# The virtual host for this application on the shared box's Caddy (docs/hosting-shared-box.md).
# Append to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, beside the other project's block, with the domain filled
# in; then `sudo systemctl reload caddy`. Caddy obtains and renews the certificates itself once
# the two names' A records point at the box, passes the Host header through, and sends
# X-Forwarded-Proto: https, which makes the login cookie Secure (docs/deployment.md, step 6).
#
# The access log is off: the application keeps nothing about its readers
# (docs/CORE_DOCUMENT.md section 8), and the proxy's log would be the one place their
# addresses were kept. The www name only redirects, so that every address readers share and
# every canonical link (ELSA_BASE_URL) carries the one bare domain.

ELSA_DOMAIN {
    log {
        output discard
    }
    encode gzip zstd
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3001
}

www.ELSA_DOMAIN {
    log {
        output discard
    }
    redir https://ELSA_DOMAIN{uri} permanent
}
